{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dependency injection dependency injection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","fileName":"Dependency Injection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dependency Injection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:31\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[ASP.NET Core Application Architecture]] [[Angular Application Architecture]] [[ASP.NET Core Page and MVC Development]] [[.NET Dependency Injection and Service Lifetimes]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["ASP.NET Core Application Architecture","Angular Application Architecture","ASP.NET Core Page and MVC Development",".NET Dependency Injection and Service Lifetimes","Angular HttpClient","Data Service","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dependency injection dependency injection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","fileName":"Dependency Injection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dependency Injection","heading":"Dependency Injection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Dependency injection supplies an object with its collaborators instead of making it construct or locate them itself. This reduces hard-coded dependencies and supports reuse, readability, configuration, and isolated testing.\n\nASP.NET Core registers application services during startup and injects them into consumers such as controllers. Angular applies the same design principle to components and services, allowing an [[Angular HttpClient]] or a custom [[Data Service]] to be supplied through a constructor.\n\nIn the inventory application, commands depend on read or write context interfaces and the .NET service provider supplies their implementations through constructor injection. Registration also specifies whether an instance is transient, scoped, or shared as a singleton; this construction policy is distinct from the business behavior of the command.\n\nIts .NET examples register abstractions and implementations with the generic host or ASP.NET Core service collection, moving object composition and lifetime selection away from business behavior that consumes the dependency.","tags":["baby"],"links":["ASP.NET Core Application Architecture","Angular Application Architecture","ASP.NET Core Page and MVC Development",".NET Dependency Injection and Service Lifetimes","Angular HttpClient","Data Service","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dependency injection dependency injection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dependency Injection.md","fileName":"Dependency Injection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dependency Injection","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]\n\n[[aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf]]\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["ASP.NET Core Application Architecture","Angular Application Architecture","ASP.NET Core Page and MVC Development",".NET Dependency Injection and Service Lifetimes","Angular HttpClient","Data Service","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}